# The concept DOI is the primary identifier because a release cannot contain
# its own version DOI: Zenodo mints that only when the release is published,
# and it reads this file's snapshot from the tag. The concept DOI always
# resolves to the newest release, so it is never stale. Each version DOI is
# added to `identifiers` in the commit after that release is published.
